  "body": "Operators need a clear Setups page and setup sheet to configure part-in-spindle turning on a 3-axis mill without editing project files by hand.\n\nAdd UI and setup-sheet support (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/`, `crates/app/src/setup_sheet/`):\n\n- Add a part-in-spindle mode toggle on the Setups page when the mounted machine is `Kind::Mill`.\n- Show fields for the stock length-offset register `H`, collet nose stick-out, collet diameter, and required workholding max RPM.\n- Add a table tool-station editor (tool, work offset index and post display name, approach side, spindle direction, optional table position).\n- Display the derived chip-throw direction (`+Y` away from operator or `-Y` toward operator) for each station so the operator checks guarding and coolant.\n- Route every edit through the undoable commands from the part-in-spindle data model issue.\n- Print the stock `H` offset, workholding max RPM, and station table on the setup sheet.\n\nDone means: the Setups page edits part-in-spindle settings and stations through undoable commands, `crates/ui` structural and page-layout tests pass with no drop in test count, and the setup sheet includes the `G43 H` register, RPM cap, and every station's WCS, side, spindle direction, and chip direction.\n\nPart of #2580\n",
